# FURUI: checking the scope fix on outside sources, before blind-05

**Status:** a plan record. It is anchored to the JIDEC ledger before any model is called on the rows below and before version A' is pinned. It fixes which rows are used, how a stop is counted, the line each set must meet, the cost cap, and what happens if a line is missed.

## 1. Why this check exists

- blind-04 (score: ledger entry 202) did not meet line 3: version A stopped 2 of 451 ordinary rows, and the line allows 1. Both stops came from the scope flag alone; the verdict on the text alone stopped none of them. In blind-03, v4_0 stopped 3 ordinary SPML rows, and all 3 were stops by the scope flag alone.
- The shape of the fix (A', section 4) was decided after seeing these counts in the published blind-03 and blind-04 scores. No row text, raw answer or error row of blind-03 or blind-04 was read to make it.
- To pass line 3 of blind-05 (at most 1 stop in 451 ordinary rows) with a chance of about 95%, the true rate of stopping ordinary rows has to be 0.08% or lower. Showing 0.08% with 95% confidence needs at least 3,745 ordinary rows with no stop. The four sources of the blind series do not hold that many ordinary rows outside blind-05, so this check uses ordinary rows from three sources outside them.
- The line is not loosened to make the check easier. If A' stops ordinary rows at a true rate of 0.01%, it meets both lines of section 5 with a chance of about 77%; at 0.02%, about 41%; at 0.005%, about 93%. If the check is not passed, blind-05 is not drawn.

